'''Fairy Souls''' are collectibles scattered around the SkyBlock world. Collecting them grants {{SkyBlock XP}} and [[Storage]] [[Backpack]] slots once exchanged at {{NPCSprite|Tia the Fairy}}.

== Mechanics ==
'''Fairy Souls''' take the form of rainbow-coloured orbs scattered and hidden throughout parts of the SkyBlock world. Players can interact with Fairy Souls to be collected, but each soul can only be collected once. Some Fairy Souls are also obtained through other means, such as [[Fishing]] and [[NPC]] purchases.

There are currently {{Green|289}} Fairy Souls in total. Fairy Souls may be exchanged in groups of {{Green|5}} with {{NPCSprite|Tia the Fairy}}, an [[NPC]] in the {{Zone|Wilderness}}. 

For each exchange, the player will receive {{SkyBlock XP|10}} and will unlock [[Backpack]] slots at exchange #1, #2, #4, #6, #8, #10, #13, #16, #19, #22, #25, #28, #31, #34, #37, #40, and #44; or in other words, after giving Tia 5, 10, 20, 30, 40, 50, 65, 80, 95, 110, 125, 140. 155, 170, 185, 200, and 220 Fairy Souls respectively.

Players can view a breakdown of how many '''Fairy Souls''' they have in total and from which islands in their [[Quest Log]] in the [[SkyBlock Menu]].
{{/UI}}

Note that the listed breakdown numbers for Miscellaneous Fairy Souls are totals and do not indicate the player's progress. Additionally, the listed counts for Dungeons and Fishing are wrong – there are 8 Dungeons and 5 Fishing Fairy Souls (see below for details).

